{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29888 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 2-Methylheptyl propanoate may interact with U373 MG, a cancer cell line. The compound is linked to the sialyltransferase CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in the synthesis of sialic acid. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, all of which are implicated in targeting U373 MG. The presence of multiple pathways converging on this enzyme and ultimately on U373 MG indicates a possible role for 2-Methylheptyl propanoate in modulating sialylation processes, which could influence cell survival and proliferation in cancer cells. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and U373 MG, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mode of action and therapeutic potential.",
